Supply Chain: a `requirements.txt` dependency declared as a version range (`litellm>=1.10`) or with no version (`flask`) now produces a finding for every advisory whose affected versions overlap the declared range, in both the Python and native resolvers. Such a finding has no single installed version to confirm, so it needs review. A range line next to a pinned copy of the same package produces no finding of its own, since the pinned copy names the installed version.
